WEBVTT

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.620
When I open sheet music,

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.330
sounds rise up glowing
and create a path in the darkness.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:27.750
I just move forward following that light...

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.370
So that I won't go off the path
and get swallowed by the darkness,

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:34.040
I just follow the path faithfully... faithfully.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.370
That's the only way I know
to play the koto right now.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.120
"#24    Beyond the Right Answer"
What? Advisor for the koto club?

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.200
Ten years ago... The first year
after I graduated from college...

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.580
After becoming a math teacher,
my dream job,

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.450
I suddenly became the advisor
for a club I'd never heard of.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:27.910
"Koto Club"
The world of music was completely
unknown to me, not to mention the koto.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:32.080
Oh, I see! I'm becoming interested!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.870
What? You haven't even heard
a koto performance yet.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:38.500
Yeah, but koto sheet music consists
of a combination of 13 numbers,

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:41.200
from one through <i>kin</i>, and symbols, right?

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.790
It looks like math, so I thought
it looked interesting.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.160
Huh?

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:48.250
I casually started learning
about the world of koto.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:52.910
Okay, I'll first listen to pieces called
"classics." There's a lot to learn!

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.370
What I found there...

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:01.830
...was a delicate, meticulous world
that seemed to be perfectly calculated.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:05.370
It was indeed a math world that
I loved, with infinite potential

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.910
contained within only 13 strings.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:13.950
Wow... I'm listening... to math right now!

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:17.580
After that, I was rapidly
sucked into the world of music.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.950
And... finally, I started creating pieces.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:25.620
They were unpopular among the students,
so no one played them, though.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.160
Maybe teenagers like modern music after all.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.830
But I like classics the most.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:36.450
The number of sounds, how they're
assembled, and their timing...

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.330
They're beautiful and efficient.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:42.290
Even after I was transferred
to a different school, I kept creating pieces.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:45.700
And then... I ended up in Hakuto's koto club.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:50.040
We got many new first-year
members this year.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:54.620
Someone may play my pieces...
I guess I'm just kidding myself.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:01.120
What?! This is my piece!

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.330
My piece... My world is coming to life?!

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:14.330
Yeah! This is how I wanted it to be played!

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:17.450
This is the perfected version of my piece!

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:19.660
Who are you?

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:23.370
Oh! Um... I'm Yamamoto,
the koto club advisor!

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:26.750
If I remember right,
he's a new member named Kanzaki...

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:31.580
I'm the one who wrote
the piece you were just playing!

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:35.790
Oh... I found the sheet music
on the shelf there, so...

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:37.500
You didn't want me to play it?

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.580
I-It's not like that at all!
Actually, I'm really happy that you did!

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:44.790
Thank you for playing it!

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.700
If you'd like, you can play other--

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:47.790
No thanks.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.000
What?! Why?!

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.330
My sound is boring. I hate it.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:01.540
Suzumori!

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:04.330
If I remember correctly,
Kanzaki is your cousin, right?

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.370
I wanna ask you something.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:11.950
Both of Mio's parents work,
so he often spent time at my place.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:16.830
My mom was learning koto,
so we started learning with her, too.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:18.700
I think we were around six then.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:22.540
I see. So you two have been playing
the koto for a long time, huh?

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:23.700
No wonder you guys are so good.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.370
Not really... But Mio is special.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:29.830
Mio can "see" sounds.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:30.700
What?!

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:36.870
It's like he knows the right answer as to how
he should play or express the piece.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.950
That's an incredible talent!

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:42.500
Yes, but Mio seems to hate it.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.750
He says that the right sounds are boring.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:50.540
The set-in-stone sounds are no fun.
So he hates his own sound.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:54.750
He's been searching for
the "sound beyond the right answer."

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.910
Kanzaki!

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:01.700
Is it true that you can see sounds?!

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:03.410
Yeah. So what?

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.950
I want you to play the pieces I create!

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:12.450
When you played my piece the other day,
I was very... very moved!

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:16.830
It was like the world I pictured started
moving exactly the way I wanted...

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.410
It was quite a shock!

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:23.200
It's not good enough for it to
"start moving exactly the way" you want.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.370
I have to go "beyond that"...

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:29.580
...or I'll never be able to be
moved by my own sound.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:35.870
I'll make a piece that will allow you
to go "beyond that"

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:40.700
because I want to hear your
"sound beyond the right answer," too!

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:45.000
So... would you entrust
that talent of yours with me?!

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:47.790
No.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:48.830
What?!

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:49.540
You scare me.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:51.910
Kanzaki!

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.250
And so, here we are.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:56.830
Oh, no... I-I-I'm so nervous!

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:00.080
You're the advisor.
You should act like one, jeez...

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:04.540
By the way, you're quitting your
teaching job after the qualifier, right?

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.790
What?! H-H-How do you know that?!

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:10.910
Everyone knows it. You're the only one
who thinks no one knows.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.080
What?!

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.500
You're taking over your family's inn, right?

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:17.330
We also know you couldn't come
to the traditional music festival--

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:21.040
not because you got the flu,
but because your dad collapsed.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.330
Are you really going to quit?

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:30.500
I made the decision after
giving it a lot of thought, so...

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.080
I see...

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:39.200
Grand Master. Let's go home.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:42.000
No performance so far was that good.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:47.000
At this rate, we can't expect much
from Satowa's school, either.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:54.910
I'll go outside and get some fresh air.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:02.660
I don't want to be here even a minute longer.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.410
You should hear their performance, too!

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:10.160
You're the only one who cannot
always face the koto, Grandmother!

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:13.700
I know what she said, but I no longer can...

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:16.200
It's too late.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:21.120
Oh, you came, too, Grandma?

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.410
Keishi!

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:28.580
Hey. We need to go
in five minutes. Get ready.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.290
Aaaahhh! I-I-I-It's time!

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:31.200
Oh crap! Oh crap!

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.040
What am I gonna do? I can't breathe.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.660
C-C-Calm down, Kota. Take a deep breath.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:36.700
<i>You </i>calm down.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.620
Hozy... Hozy...!

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.700
H-Hey, guys! After leaving this room,
we can't speak loudly,

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.080
so do you wanna form a circle?

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.910
Yeah! That's a good idea!

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:46.750
I wanna do it!

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:48.450
It'll give us power!

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:50.160
Oh, Mr. Takinami and Miss Akira, if you'd--

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.450
No way.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:52.950
I'm okay.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.870
Oh, it's kinda embarrassing.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.200
This is fun!

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:00.410
Whoa... I feel...

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:04.330
...the warmth from the other guys...
It kinda calms me down.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:09.290
Hey, four-eyes! Say something!

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:12.330
Oh, yeah. Of course.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:16.700
Um... I want to continue playing
with you guys for a little while longer.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:19.200
I don't want today to be
our last day playing together!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.750
So let's play with all--

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:21.750
What was that for?!

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.330
Hey! Stop saying depressing stuff!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.500
Say something to get us fired up!

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:29.790
If you're gonna do it, say something
you usually can't with all your might!

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.040
Shout it!

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:36.080
We're gonna go to nationals for sure!

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:39.700
Yeah!

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:48.160
Oh... Finally, Hakuto is next.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.450
The school who won last time, right?

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:51.370
Yep.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:54.250
If they give a performance that's
like the right answer like last time,

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:57.080
Tokise can win.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:59.580
But if it's different from last time...

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.660
"Hakuto"

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.450
Okay, guys! Do your best!

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:10.950
You don't have to tell us. We will!

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:13.120
The pieces you create are plain,

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:16.040
but we'll prove that...

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:18.500
...they're actually amazing!

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:21.000
We'll get the ticket to nationals
as a farewell gift for you.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.830
Look forward to it!

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:39.790
Program number 12. Hakuto High School.

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:41.540
"Katakago."

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:44.750
I've hated my own sound all this time.

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:46.910
It's the right answer,
but something is missing.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:50.120
It's not wrong, but it's somewhat boring.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:53.080
I've been searching for
this missing something...

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:54.160
But...

00:10:57.700 --> 00:10:59.200
Thanks...

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:03.330
Thanks to all of you,
I can finally go to the other side...

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:13.750
What a deep first sound...

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.700
Is this a classical piece...?

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:34.580
No, if I remember right,
it should be an original piece.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:39.620
What a tranquil space...

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:43.120
It's like if I exhale, people might hear it.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.870
Frankly speaking, it's very plain.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:50.660
It doesn't have the lively feeling
of high school students, either. But...

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.250
Again...

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:57.910
It's not like it's got momentum,
nor does it have a catchy melody,

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:01.330
but his sound just flows into my head.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:03.500
I can't take my eyes off of him.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:10.080
A performance that's as if it's
the right answer to the piece...

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:16.950
This is, indeed, incredible. This isn't
a performance by high school students.

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:20.750
But that's thanks in large part
to the piece itself.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:28.250
The solo and the three other parts...

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:32.410
How the sounds are placed
and intertwined is impeccable.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:35.290
Though it seems the difference in ability
between the guy in the center

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:37.500
and the rest is quite big,

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:41.500
the piece was solidly calculated
so that it's well-balanced

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:43.870
while making the solo stand out.

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:47.330
The tempo that makes
people feel comfortable...

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:51.870
The pauses that draw you in... To think
someone could create a piece like this...

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.160
How scary...

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:58.620
It's true that their level is quite high.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:03.830
It's not just the piece.
It's amazing that they can express it.

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:10.410
But after hearing that performance
by Himesaka, something is missing.

00:13:12.250 --> 00:13:14.500
I'll quit the koto.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:18.700
What?! Why? You liked how
the koto sounded, didn't you?

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:24.000
I like the sound of the koto. But when I play,
it becomes a sound I don't like.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.790
When I play, the sound of the koto dies.

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:29.410
It dies?

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.200
Listen, Mio. I don't understand it much,

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:39.620
but no one can play the sound
they want from the start.

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:40.870
Really?

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:42.410
Yeah, I think...

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:45.160
Then when will I be able
to play the sound I like?

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:48.750
That... probably depends on
how much effort you put in.

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:50.450
Effort?

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:56.120
Will playing a lot do? If I play all day long,
will it become a sound I like?

00:13:56.120 --> 00:14:02.160
A sound that's free and independent
from everything, like water and wind...

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.950
A sound with life...

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:08.700
It'd make me happy if I could
create a sound like that...

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:14.700
But after a year, three years,
even five years...

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:17.620
In all that time, I was never able
to play a sound like that.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:20.120
Mio, I think you're thinking too much.

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:22.870
You're very good. Have confidence.

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:24.910
Would you like to participate
in a competition?

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:26.950
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:31.910
Hey, Mio. Everyone praises your sound.
They say you're very good. So--

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:33.870
I don't care about "everyone."

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:38.410
I just want to create
the sound I like by myself!

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:40.370
Mio...

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:45.540
I feel kinda upset.
I don't know what to do.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:52.620
I can always see the sounds, but they
never lead me to the place I wanna go...

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.660
I'm tired...

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.290
I'm exhausted.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:57.620
I'll...

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:01.290
I'll make a piece that will allow you
to go "beyond that"

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:05.290
because I want to hear your "sound
beyond the right answer," too!

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:10.040
It was a shock... like a dazzling light...

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:16.290
The sound changed?

00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:18.120
You create pieces by calculating?

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.040
That's right!

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.830
I don't like calculated sounds.

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:25.790
Then I'll make it sound
uncalculated by calculating!

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:31.250
How's this piece?

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:33.540
It's fine.

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:34.660
I'll rewrite it!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:35.620
What?

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:39.910
I promised you I'd make a piece that
will allow you to go "beyond that."

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:43.540
So the piece has to be
something you want to play!

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:49.830
You can only play the sound
the way you see it?

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:54.450
Yeah. I don't know how to play
the other sounds.

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:57.080
The sound I can see glows
and becomes a path.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:00.700
But the area around it is pitch-dark
and there's nothing there.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:05.120
If I go off the path, I'm gonna
fall into the darkness for sure.

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:11.870
The moment you go off the path, though,
I think a new path is created.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:15.620
And then, this time,
<i>you </i>will become the path!

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:21.870
What's this unnerving feeling...?

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:26.750
Hey, hey, hey...! The solo part has
been repeating only one sound.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:32.080
And... just how deep is he
going to dive with it...?

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:37.250
I don't quite get what Mr. Yamamoto said.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:39.950
They're disorganized.
Their sound is messy.

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:43.700
If I go off the path, I bet I'll be just like--

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:57.120
What...? What's with this sound...?

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:58.910
Their feelings are flowing into me...

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:02.160
...even though I don't know
anything about these people.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:05.330
Everyone's smiling. They're happy and alive.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:08.040
It's as if they <i>themselves </i>are the sound...

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.790
<i>You </i>will become the path!

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.330
Clearly...

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:31.330
...there's something happening... right now...

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.410
Mio...

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:05.870
Hey...!

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:07.410
What's going on?!

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:13.160
I'm getting dragged into it!

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:21.370
Ahh... Amazing...

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:22.870
This is amazing...

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:28.120
Within only 13 strings,
they're creating a boundless universe!

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.580
Hey, Mio!

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:32.290
This piece isn't just yours!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.540
Don't forget about us!

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:37.910
I'm sorry, Club President.
It's just that I'm having fun.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:41.950
I'll take you guys with me... anywhere...

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:44.200
There are only 13 strings.

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:49.040
But even so, I can now go wherever
I want, to the ends of the earth...

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:03.160
I heard that Mr. Yamamoto is going
to quit teaching after the qualifier.

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:06.790
His dad collapsed.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:10.330
Let's make sure our last performance
for him is a good one.

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:20.950
Hey, Kanzaki. Do you know what
kind of flower a <i>katakago </i>is?

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:22.450
No, I don't.

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:26.910
It's a flower that can't bloom
one year, three years,

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:30.330
or even five years after budding.

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:40.120
Even so, it keeps growing
little by little every year

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:44.870
and finally blooms after
almost ten long years.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.700
Say, Kanzaki...

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:58.080
It's been ten years since we
came to know the koto, huh?

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:50.910
It was like something awakened
in him at the end...

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:54.910
So you can play the koto like this too, huh?

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:58.910
Oh, crap. I'm getting nervous again
after hearing Hakuto's performance...

00:21:58.910 --> 00:22:02.000
Seriously! Why do we have
to play after Hakuto?

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:06.330
Rhythm... Rhythm... I hope I can
stay together with everyone else.

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:09.160
I hope my fingers move okay!

00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:15.000
Everyone is so nervous.
I have to say something.

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:17.290
What?

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:24.330
We'll be fine. We don't have
to worry about anything.

00:22:24.330 --> 00:22:26.290
We'll be fine if we just play
like we always do.

00:22:26.290 --> 00:22:28.250
Takezo...

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:35.120
Because we've practiced...

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:37.450
...more than anyone for sure!

00:22:42.620 --> 00:22:45.000
If our club president says so,
then it must be true!

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:46.910
Hey, Kudo!

00:22:46.910 --> 00:22:49.450
You'll be fine.

00:22:49.450 --> 00:22:52.580
You survived my tough lessons.

00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:56.160
So please play to your heart's content today.

00:22:56.160 --> 00:22:58.120
Miss Aki...

00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:00.580
Tokise High School.
Please proceed to the stage.

00:23:00.580 --> 00:23:01.500
Okay!

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:04.580
Don't forget.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:07.750
What's important isn't
going to nationals itself,

00:23:07.750 --> 00:23:10.080
but <i>why </i>you want to go to nationals.

00:23:10.080 --> 00:23:11.290
Don't forget that.

00:23:12.540 --> 00:23:14.330
Why...

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:16.120
...do we want to...

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:20.910
If you lose in the next qualifier,
they won't be able to go to nationals.

00:23:20.910 --> 00:23:24.870
So to them, it's their last chance.

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:27.250
I don't want it to end yet.

00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:29.660
I wish it could go on forever.

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:32.700
Next year won't work for you guys!

00:23:32.700 --> 00:23:35.660
Next year... will be too late.

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:38.620
We're gonna go to nationals for sure!

00:23:50.120 --> 00:23:51.950
Next time, "Tenkyu."

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:54.540
"#25   Tenkyu"
